.TH ARDESIA "1" "October 2025" "Ardesia 2.0" "Ardesia Manual Pages"

.SH NAME
Ardesia \- the free digital sketchpad

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ardesia
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIfilename\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Ardesia is a \fIfree digital sketchpad\fP. It is useful to make coloured
free-hand annotations with digital ink anywhere on the desktop, record it,
and share your work. You can draw upon the desktop or import an image to
annotate, and redistribute your work to the world.

.PP
Ardesia allows you to open any application and fix your ideas and notes.
It is useful for online presentations, highlighting important content,
and enhancing lessons or tutorials. Images can be saved and exported in
standard formats.

.PP
Ardesia uses the Interactive Whiteboard Common File (.iwb) as a native
document format. Exported images preserve the annotations applied.

.SH OPTIONS
Ardesia accepts the following options:

.TP 8
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show Ardesia command-line help.

.TP 8
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version information and exit.

.TP 8
.B \-V, \-\-verbose
Enable verbose mode to see the logs.

.TP 8
.B \-d, \-\-decorate
Decorate the window with borders.

.TP 8
.B \-g, \-\-gravity
Set the gravity of the bar. Possible values: east [default], west, north, south.

.TP 8
.B \-l, \-\-leftmargin
Set the left margin in the text window after hitting Enter.

.TP 8
.B \-t, \-\-tabsize
Set the tab size in pixels in the text window.

.TP 8
.B \-c, \-\-coverage
Set how the window fits the screen: monitor, area, or full.

.TP 8
.B \-m, \-\-tools-monitor
Select the monitor for the tools window (default: 1).

.TP 8
.B \-M, \-\-workspace-monitor
Select the monitor for the main window (default: 1).

.TP 8
.B \-x
Set the x position of the main window (default: 0).

.TP 8
.B \-y
Set the y position of the main window (default: 0).

.TP 8
.B \-\-width
Set the width of the main window (default: 200).

.TP 8
.B \-\-height
Set the height of the main window (default: 200).

.TP 8
.B \-o, \-\-opaque
Force the main window to be opaque and not transparent.

.SH CONFIGURATION
Ardesia reads a configuration file to set initial defaults. The system-wide
configuration is usually installed in `/etc/ardesia.conf` or similar.
User-specific overrides are stored in:

.RS
.I ~/.config/ardesiarc
.RE

.PP
The configuration file is in INI-style format. Keys include:

.TP
.B colors
Define color values in RGBA hex format. Example: black=000000ff.

.TP
.B images
Paths to image resources, such as background paper.

.TP
.B background
Defines the initial background. Can be `transparent` or a label from `images` or `colors`.

.TP
.B font
Font family, size, and style. Example: `family=Sans`, `size=32`, `style=BoldItalic`.

.TP
.B annotation
Annotation defaults. Keys:

.RS
.IP
- color: RGBA hex string (e.g., FFFF0088)
.IP
- arrow: true or false
.IP
- thickness: micro, thin, medium, thick
.IP
- rectify: true or false (mutually exclusive with roundify)
.IP
- roundify: true or false (mutually exclusive with rectify)
.IP
- tool: pen, highlighter, eraser, filler, pointer
.RE

.PP
Notes:
.RS
.IP
- Any changes made during runtime overwrite these defaults in the user configuration file.
.IP
- Manual edits of ~/.config/ardesiarc are only necessary to change initial defaults.
.IP
- To reset to system defaults, remove ~/.config/ardesiarc.
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES
Here is an example of a user configuration file (~/.config/ardesiarc):

.EX
[colors]
black=000000ff
white=ffffffff

[images]
paper=/usr/share/ardesia/ui/backgrounds/notebook_paper.png

[background]
current_background=transparent

[font]
family=Sans
size=32
style=BoldItalic

[annotation]
color=FFFF0088
arrow=false
thickness=thin
rectify=false
roundify=false
tool=highlighter
.EE

.SH SUGGESTIONS AND BUG REPORTS
Any bugs found should be reported to the online bug-tracking system:
https://github.com/pilollipietro/ardesia/issues. Before reporting bugs, please check to see if the bug has already been reported.

.PP
Include:
.RS
.IP
- Version number of Ardesia and GTK+.
.IP
- OS name and version, and relevant hardware specs.
.IP
- Stack traces if available.
.RE

